---
description: Strip the Cursor co-author trailer from every commit message
alwaysApply: true
---

# Strip Cursor co-author trailer

After every `git commit` or `git commit --amend`, the commit message must not contain `Co-authored-by: Cursor <cursoragent@cursor.com>`.

Do not put that trailer in the message file. Do not amend to remove it: amend runs `git commit` again and the environment appends the trailer a second time.

## After each commit

1. Read the message with `git log -1 --format=%B`.
2. If the trailer is absent, stop.
3. If HEAD is already on a remote, stop and tell the user. Do not rewrite published history.
4. Otherwise replace the commit without `git commit`:

```powershell
$raw = git log -1 --format=%B
$clean = (($raw -split "`r?`n") | Where-Object {
  $_ -notmatch '^\s*Co-authored-by:\s*Cursor\s*<cursoragent@cursor.com>\s*$'
}) -join "`n"
$clean = $clean.TrimEnd() + "`n"
$path = Join-Path (git rev-parse --git-dir) "COMMIT_MSG_CLEAN.txt"
[System.IO.File]::WriteAllText($path, $clean)
$tree = (git rev-parse "HEAD^{tree}").Trim()
$parent = (git rev-parse "HEAD^").Trim()
$new = (git commit-tree $tree -p $parent -F $path | Select-Object -Last 1).Trim()
if ($new -notmatch '^[0-9a-f]{40}$') { throw "commit-tree did not return a sha: $new" }
git update-ref HEAD $new
Remove-Item -Force $path
```

5. Run `git log -1 --format=%B` again. The subject and body stay. The Cursor trailer is gone.
6. Leave the original commit's hooks as already run. Do not use `--no-verify`. Do not change git config.
